From 4892097d0a2af67d07d20690bcad3f965fae8fb4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arena-ai-coding-agent <arena-ai-coding-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 07:38:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Point OpenCode Zen adapter directly at the anonymous Zen
 route

The installer was wiring the adapter to the loopback shim (127.0.0.1:8791),
so a normal install failed at the first completion unless the operator also
ran zen_shim.js. Configure the bridge to talk directly to
https://opencode.ai/zen/v1 (anonymous, no API key), normalize the adapter
source so its own default matches, and include the failing endpoint URL in
TRANSPORT errors so unreachable/blocked upstreams are diagnosable. The shim
remains available as an optional baseURL override.
---
 README.md                     |  6 +++---
 docs/index.html               |  5 ++---
 install.sh                    |  8 +++++---
 tools/enable-opencode-zen.mjs | 19 ++++++++++++++++---
 4 files changed, 26 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 1fca0d9..9048d15 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -23,19 +23,19 @@ BUILD=0 ./install.sh "$HOME/dsh-remote-web"
 
 ### Opt-in OpenCode Zen bridge
 
-Pass `OPENCODE_ZEN=1` to also add the [DSH OpenCode Zen bridge](https://github.com/DHS-M/dsh-opencode-zen) from the same organization. It installs only the standalone `@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm-opencode` model adapter and points the default agent model at `opencode-zen` / `big-pickle` through a local loopback route. Web-search plugins are intentionally excluded.
+Pass `OPENCODE_ZEN=1` to also add the [DSH OpenCode Zen bridge](https://github.com/DHS-M/dsh-opencode-zen) from the same organization. It installs only the standalone `@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm-opencode` model adapter and points the default agent model at `opencode-zen` / `big-pickle` (anonymous, no API key) directly against `https://opencode.ai/zen/v1`. Web-search plugins are intentionally excluded.
 
 ```bash
 OPENCODE_ZEN=1 BUILD=1 ./install.sh "$HOME/dsh-remote-web"
 ```
 
-Start the Zen shim (or any OpenAI-compatible endpoint) before using the route:
+The adapter needs no local shim by default. If your network blocks `opencode.ai` or you prefer the repo's loopback shim, point the adapter's `baseURL` at `http://127.0.0.1:8791/v1` and run:
 
 ```bash
 node <dsh-opencode-zen>/zen_shim.js
 ```
 
-If you are not calling the real OpenCode Zen endpoint, the bridge still works against an OpenAI-compatible `/v1` server bound to `http://127.0.0.1:8791`.
+For any other OpenAI-compatible `/v1` server, set `baseURL` to that endpoint.
 
 The enable step also normalizes the upstream standalone adapter's SSE tool-call name handling (`state.name += …` → `state.name = …`). Without that fix a normal one-chunk `web_search` tool call is recorded as `web_searchweb_search` and rejected as an unknown tool. The adapter still removes the DSH-incompatible `export default apply` so the Cordis loader reads its named `inject`/`name` metadata.
 
